    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="0689" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/225</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Lend-Lease
                        Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-11">February 11,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Stettinius</hi>: In view of the efforts
                    which the Turkish Government is now making to prepare for the possible extension
                    of hostilities in the Near East during the spring, the Department of State
                    regards it as particularly important that supplies be furnished to <pb
                        facs="0690" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/> Turkey as soon as possible, not only
                    for the purpose of strengthening the Turkish Government in its announced
                    determination to resist aggression but also in order to enable that resistance
                    to be effective.</p>
                <p>This Department understands that the Turkish military authorities consider it of
                    the greatest importance, for instance, that 950 trucks, for which the Turkish
                    Government has already deposited more than $1,000,000 in cash payment, reach
                    Turkey by the end of March.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
